cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SvanBot in your own work, please cite it as below."
title: SvanBot
abstract: >-
  SvanBot is a self-hosted, fully autonomous poker bot fleet for openpoker.ai: 6-max no-limit
  hold'em with virtual chips and 14-day seasons. It plays up to five portfolio bots from one
  machine, and each decision is an exploitative expected-value search — every legal action priced
  against the ranges each opponent has actually shown, rather than a precomputed equilibrium. A
  separate learner process keeps tuning the policy on paired, luck-reduced simulations and promotes
  a change only when the change wins on fresh deals. It runs on CPU only, with no GPU required.
authors:
  - name: The SvanBot authors
    alias: SvanLabs
type: software
version: 10.0.0
# Dual-licensed, "MIT OR Apache-2.0" at your option. CFF 1.2.0 has no field for an SPDX
# expression, so the two identifiers are listed separately, which it defines as a choice between
# them — the same thing `Cargo.toml` and the two `LICENSE-*` files say.
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/SvanLabs/SvanBot
keywords:
  - poker
  - no-limit hold'em
  - openpoker.ai
  - opponent modeling
  - monte carlo
  - rust
